# Atlas scan

The OPDP atlas cut into records without being parsed whole (parsed whole, the
85 MB release 1.2 takes 19.4 s and 1.95 GB; release 1.8 is twelve times larger).
A byte scanner keeps a few integers of state across chunks and cuts out each
element of the top-level `records` array as one compact line; the rest is kept
as the header, the array emptied, so its declared record count can be checked.

## An AtlasScan has:
    a depth, which is Int.
    an inString, which is Bool.
    an escaped, which is Bool.
    an inRecords, which is Bool.
    an inRecord, which is Bool.
    a keyBytes, which is Seq of Int.
    a lastKey, which is Text.
    a recordBytes, which is Seq of Int.
    a headerBytes, which is Seq of Int.
    a records, which is Seq of Text.
    a count, which is Int.

## To newAtlasScan () -> AtlasScan:
    Return a new AtlasScan with depth 0 and inString false and escaped false and inRecords false and inRecord false and keyBytes [] and lastKey "" and records [] and count 0.

## Note
The scan after the next piece of the document. The array after the key `records`
at depth one is THE records array; whitespace between tokens is dropped.

## To scanChunk (st: AtlasScan, bytes: Seq of Int) -> AtlasScan:
    Let mutable out be st.
    Let mutable depth be st's depth.
    Let mutable inString be st's inString.
    Let mutable escaped be st's escaped.
    Let mutable inRecords be st's inRecords.
    Let mutable inRecord be st's inRecord.
    Let mutable key be copy of st's keyBytes.
    Let mutable rec be copy of st's recordBytes.
    Let mutable header be copy of st's headerBytes.
    Let mutable done be copy of st's records.
    Repeat for b in bytes:
        Let wasString be inString.
        Let atTop be depth is equal to 1 and inRecords is equal to false.
        If wasString:
            If escaped:
                Set escaped to false.
            Otherwise:
                If b is equal to 92:
                    Set escaped to true.
                If b is equal to 34:
                    Set inString to false.
                    If atTop:
                        Set out's lastKey to text_from_bytes(key).
                If b is not equal to 92 and b is not equal to 34 and atTop:
                    Push b to key.
        Otherwise:
            If b is equal to 34:
                Set inString to true.
                Set key to [].
            If b is equal to 123 or b is equal to 91:
                Set depth to depth + 1.
                If inRecords and depth is equal to 3:
                    Set inRecord to true.
                    Set rec to [].
        If wasString or (b is not equal to 32 and b is not equal to 10 and b is not equal to 13 and b is not equal to 9):
            If inRecord:
                Push b to rec.
            If inRecord is equal to false and inRecords is equal to false:
                Push b to header.
        If wasString is equal to false and (b is equal to 125 or b is equal to 93):
            Set depth to depth - 1.
            If inRecord and depth is equal to 2:
                Push text_from_bytes(rec) to done.
                Set inRecord to false.
            If inRecords and depth is equal to 1:
                Set inRecords to false.
                Push 93 to header.
        If wasString is equal to false and b is equal to 91 and depth is equal to 2 and inRecords is equal to false and out's lastKey is equal to "records":
            Set inRecords to true.
    Let mutable next be a new AtlasScan with depth depth and inString inString and escaped escaped and inRecords inRecords and inRecord inRecord and keyBytes key.
    Set next's lastKey to out's lastKey.
    Set next's recordBytes to rec.
    Set next's headerBytes to header.
    Set next's records to done.
    Set next's count to st's count + length of done - length of st's records.
    Return next.

## To scanComplete (st: AtlasScan) -> Bool:
    Return st's depth is equal to 0 and st's inString is equal to false and st's inRecord is equal to false.

## To scanInPieces (doc: Text, pieceSize: Int) -> AtlasScan:
    Let bs be text_bytes(doc).
    Let mutable st be newAtlasScan().
    Let mutable start be 1.
    While start is at most length of bs:
        Let upto be start + pieceSize - 1.
        If upto is greater than length of bs:
            Set st to scanChunk(st, items start through (length of bs) of bs).
        Otherwise:
            Set st to scanChunk(st, items start through upto of bs).
        Set start to upto + 1.
    Return st.

## Test: records come out compact, strings keep their spaces, the header stays, and a nested records key is not the array

Let doc be "{{\n  \"name\": \"U\",\n  \"records\": [\n    {{ \"id\" : 1 , \"t\" : \"a  b \\\" {{[ c\" }},\n    {{\"id\": 2}}\n  ],\n  \"tail\": 1\n}}\n".
Let st be scanInPieces(doc, 1000000).
Expect that st's records is equal to ["{{\"id\":1,\"t\":\"a  b \\\" {{[ c\"}}", "{{\"id\":2}}"].
Expect that text_from_bytes(st's headerBytes) is equal to "{{\"name\":\"U\",\"records\":[],\"tail\":1}}".
Expect that scanComplete(st) and st's count is equal to 2.
Let deeper be scanInPieces("{{\"meta\": {{\"records\": [{{\"x\": 1}}]}}, \"records\": [{{\"problem_id\": 9}}]}}", 5).
Expect that deeper's records is equal to ["{{\"problem_id\":9}}"].

## Test: the scan does not depend on where the chunks are cut

For all booleans tiny:
    Let doc be "{{\"records\": [{{\"a\": \"x, y\"}}, {{\"b\": [1, {{\"c\": 2}}]}}], \"n\": 2}}".
    Let mutable size be 7.
    If tiny:
        Set size to 1.
    Expect that (scanInPieces(doc, size))'s records is equal to (scanInPieces(doc, 1000))'s records.
